 {"status": "complete", "id": "AUG-148", "title": "Symlinked spec files are followed out of the corpus root, while <include src> outside the root is refused", "detail": {"fingerprint": "b500c7e493f3caee48b8bc4b5b4ee649e488348aea7fd66cd956f100cd93150e", "evidence": [{"run_id": "f12e309e", "ts": "2026-11-13T15:58:19.606984+00:00"}]}, "priority": "P3", "source": null, "reasoning": "Deep pass 2026-11-05 at cf5bfe2: with linked.xml -> /etc/hostname inside the corpus, `spec validate` reads and parses the target ('spec error (invalid-xml): linked.xml: syntax error'), i.e. the loader followed a symlink outside the root and consumed host-file bytes. By contrast <include src=\"/etc/hostname\"/> is refused with remote-reference-rejected ('only repository-relative local files are allowed'). The out-of-root rule is therefore enforced on one mechanism and bypassable on the other.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: a symlink whose target resolves outside the corpus root is refused with a typed error (or skipped with an explicit count), proven by a fixture that links to a file outside the root.\nPASS: a symlink whose target stays inside the root keeps working (no over-blocking), proven by the paired positive fixture.\nPASS: the rule is stated once and applied to both mechanisms — include and file discovery — and a test asserts both paths produce the same class of refusal.\nPASS: no host-file content can reach stdout/stderr beyond the typed diagnostic naming the path (asserted by grepping the error text for target content).", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:24:13.639428+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-13T15:58:19.606984+00:00", "foreman_note": "2026-11-05 wave: merged on main 6b0d190 (spec-a 7bb5565/c6b24b3/c84f617, spec-b 4b27c83/8375d78/35267f6, corpus 20731e8); full gate on merged tree GATE PASS rc=0, 485 passed/2 skipped, live arms 2/0; targeted 113 passed; verdict still outstanding (no fabricated run id)\n\n2026-11-13 driver: NOT clos