 {"status": "complete", "id": "AUG-149", "title": "A no-match selection returns rc 0 with empty output and no diagnostic", "detail": {"fingerprint": "853e1f9ba0a77f73768420a99a94a1378b0ee160161e3de97694e81c9d789d5a", "evidence": [{"run_id": "277112c1", "ts": "2026-11-13T16:20:47.549045+00:00"}]}, "priority": "P4", "source": null, "reasoning": "Deep pass 2026-11-05 at cf5bfe2: `auger spec list <corpus> --applies-to nope.none` exits 0 with zero bytes on stdout and nothing on stderr, and the same holds for `--version 3.0.0`. The PRD's finding taxonomy names 'no match' as a reportable selection finding, and a caller scripting the CLI cannot distinguish 'your selector matched nothing' from 'the tool had nothing to say' without parsing emptiness. The empty-selector case is already refused correctly ('empty-selector'), so the contract is inconsistent between the two shapes.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: a selector that matches nothing reports it explicitly (a one-line notice on stderr or a typed empty result with a count of 0) while keeping stdout machine-parseable; asserted by a test on both `spec list` and `spec assemble`.\nPASS: the exit code contract is stated in the README/help and matches behaviour for the three shapes: no selector, selector with no match, selector with matches.\nPASS: existing consumers are not broken by the change: `--format json` still emits a valid document with an empty selection and exit code 0 unless the README says otherwise.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:24:13.725478+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-13T16:20:47.549045+00:00", "foreman_note": "2026-11-05 wave: merged on main 6b0d190 (spec-a 7bb5565/c6b24b3/c84f617, spec-b 4b27c83/8375d78/35267f6, corpus 20731e8); full gate on merged tree GATE PASS rc=0, 485 passed/2 skipped, live arms 2/0; targeted 113 passed; verdict still outstanding (no fabricated run id)\n\n2026-11-13 driver: judged PASS at bd506c3. Verdict .gitreins/history/2026-11-13/2