 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-153", "title": "GitReins' spec_alignment guard is enabled in no repo, so the now-implemented Auger checker is never invoked", "detail": {"fingerprint": "0f4f3852b731a6d5e9510b1bf9a6824ef99113e2afbb5f830c1cb26212e58265", "evidence": []}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "MEASURED 2026-11-05 at main e1adcd3 (after SG5 landed AUG-135/AUG-120): the Auger half of the seam now exists and answers GitReins' exact argv, but NOTHING invokes it, so the seam still executes zero times in production.\nEvidence:\n- `grep -rn spec_alignment /home/kara/gitreins/.gitreins/config.yaml` -> no match. The block is absent, so dataclass defaults apply (engine/config.py:73-84): enabled=False, command='', spec_root='specs', mode='warn', missing_checker='warn', protocol_version='1', min_checker_version='1.0.0'. engine/guard_manager.py:1858 gates the whole path on `spec_alignment.enabled is True`.\n- `grep -rl spec_alignment /home/kara/*/.gitreins/config.yaml` -> exactly one repo: /home/kara/monitoring/.gitreins/config.yaml lines 23-32, and it is `enabled: false` with `command: ''`.\n- Auger side proven working in the same session: `git diff --cached | auger.py spec align --repo-root <repo> --spec-root <specs> --protocol-version 1 --diff-stdin` -> one compact JSON line (status/scope/findings), and `auger spec check --diff-stdin` returns a byte-identical payload.\nSo the failure mode this row names is not \"the checker is missing\" (AUG-135) but \"the guard is armed nowhere\" - a config decision in a consumer repo, which is why it is filed separately instead of being folded into SG5.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: one consumer repo (pilot: /home/kara/monitoring, the only repo that already carries a spec_alignment block; auger is acceptable if the owner prefers) has `spec_alignment.enabled: true` and a non-empty `command` naming the auger binary and `--repo-root/--spec-root/--protocol-version/--diff-stdin`. Verify